6915a6c4130105d1d9219d7254e7162e6713d8bd30206eea8f","event_uuid":"359a167b-38f8-41aa-8cbf-f9c47ba8e303","position":{"commit_sha":"225f781868cef1f1b1cf1eb641622763e434d562","position":"1795118827072539527-359a167b-38f8-41aa-8cbf-f9c47ba8e303"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"08a5af14a3bec88a46c9cf337835ea09959502bec42594ef139d67bdb1a49013","event_uuid":"2825ad26-8a86-44c1-9f9a-151ada70c6a5","position":{"commit_sha":"225f781868cef1f1b1cf1eb641622763e434d562","position":"1795118827110744990-2825ad26-8a86-44c1-9f9a-151ada70c6a5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795112637875527528,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\nAfter the sibling story that adds `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` and sets it in the MCP deployment, the server verifies op-certs against its own list. The rest of rebar still reads the repo-pinned `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`: the verify trust root (`_opcert_trust_root`, `_pinned_environment_keys`, `_rotated_own_key_verdict` in `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`), the signing refusal (`_pinned_public_key_bodies`, `_refuse_if_pinned_principal_key_mismatch` in `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`, called at line 366), the health fallback in `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`, and the merge gate `rebar verify-opcert` (`src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`, calling `trusted_env.verify_required_environment` at line 192). Per ADR 0125 the default is validity-only and signing is never gated on an allowed key. This story stops every code path reading the pin file; the next sibling deletes the file and command. Sequencing: built on the trust-list story's merged commit.\n\n## Approach\n1. `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`: no list means the trust root is the SSHSIG's embedded key for the certificate's principal (trust basis `envelope_key`); a list applies the existing list check (`trust_list` or `untrusted`). Delete `_opcert_trust_root`, `_pinned_environment_keys`, `_rotated_own_key_verdict`; rotation needs no special case because the embedded key verifies its own signature. `verify.require_environment` set requires principal equality AND a list, else `foreign_key` with a reason saying a list is required. Results keep `signing_key` and `key_id` (the environment).\n2. `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`: delete `_pinned_public_key_bodies`, `_refuse_if_pinned_principal_key_mismatch` and its call, so signing never consults trust configuration. Delete `_warn_if_verify_cannot_resolve` and `_opcert_own_public_keys`: the warning exists only because the old verify path trusted the environment's own key files, which no verify path uses afterwards (confirm with Serena references plus `git grep -nF` per name before deleting).\n3. `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`: drop the pin-file branch and its `trust_source: \"pin_file\"` value; `expected` is true only when the list is set.\n4. `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`: verify each closed ticket's completion-verifier certificate with a new helper `verify_completion_opcert(envelope, bound, ticket_id, material, merged_commit, *, required_env, trusted_keys)` in `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`: principal equals `required_env`, (principal, key) listed, signature verifies under that key, and the signed subject digest equals `rebar.attest.opcert.opcert_subject_digest(ticket_id, material, merged_commit, \"completion-verifier\")`. Keep the authoritative-material recompute and the merged-commit ancestry check; remove the storage-anchor lookup (`_opcert_anchor_event`) and era arguments, which served only pin-file key eras. Required environment without a list exits 2 naming both keys. Move the per-ticket check into a helper so `cli` stays at or below its complexity ceiling of 20. The imports of `_collect_all`, `_is_enforced`, `_resolve_commit` from `verify_authorship.py` stay unchanged (that file belongs to starving-sphalerite-skua and is not edited).\n5. `trust_basis` becomes `envelope_key | trust_list | null` in `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json` (description updated); regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` with `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`; update the trust-basis prose in `docs/reuse-surface.md` and the `verify_signature` ToolSpec in `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py` with its copy in `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json`; update help in `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`; regenerate `docs/cli-reference.md`.\n6. Rewrite op-cert tests that build pin files to use the list or validity-only; delete modules that test only removed behaviour.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`, `src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py`\n- `src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json`, `src/rebar/types.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, `tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json`, `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt`, `docs/cli-reference.md`\n- tests edited: `tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py`, `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py`, `tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_rollback.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py`, `tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py`\n- tests deleted: `tests/unit/test_opcert_own_principal_rotation_d909.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py`\nOut of scope: deleting the pin file, `src/rebar/attest/trusted_env.py` and `rebar trusted-env` (next sibling); prose docs and runbooks (docs sibling). `rebar.attest.opcert.verify_opcert` stays as a library primitive.\n\n## Testing\nNo list: a validly signed certificate from any key is `certified` with `envelope_key`, `signing_key` and `key_id`; tampered payload, cross-ticket or cross-kind replay is `mismatch`; undecodable envelope is `invalid`; a certificate under a rotated-out own key verifies. List set: listed passes, unlisted is `untrusted`. `require_environment` without a list gives `foreign_key`; with a list and a listed key of that environment, `certified`. Signing succeeds for a key on no list. `verify-opcert`: listed completion cert passes; unlisted fails exit 1; required environment without a list exits 2; no required environment is advisory exit 0. Health: list unset gives `expected` false.\nPortability: removes code; remaining checks use the existing `ssh-keygen` path; no new subprocess, fd, path or permission handling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With no trust setting, op-cert verification passes a validly signed certificate from any key, fails a tampered or wrongly bound certificate, and reports `signing_key` and the environment (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py -q`).\n- [ ] Signing succeeds for a key that is on no list (checked: a test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`).\n- [ ] `rebar verify-opcert` verifies completion certificates against the trust list with no pin file (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py -q`).\n- [ ] `git grep -nF trusted_env -- src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py` prints no hits.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] After autodeploy rolls this change, the live MCP `/health` `opcert` field still reads `expected: true`, `matched: true`, `trust_source: \"trust_list\"` and no `error`.\n  provenance: environment=rebar Gerrit box i-00880b2c7f13527c5; principal=operator AWS profile frontier; privilege_posture=read-only SSM command running curl against the MCP loopback /health; instrument=aws ssm send-command + get-command-invocation — the health route is loopback-only, so no repository check can observe the deployed container.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the change lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py","reason":"validity-only default; remove pinned trust root; verify_completion_opcert"},{"path":"src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py","reason":"remove pinned-key signing refusal and own-key verify warning"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py","reason":"drop pin-file branch"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py","reason":"verify completion certs against trust list"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/verify_signature_result.schema.json","reason":"trust_basis enum"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py","reason":"verify_signature description"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"trust_basis prose"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/mcp_tool_surface_golden.json","reason":"embedded description"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/verify.py","reason":"verify-opcert help"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/verify-opcert.txt","reason":"generated help"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_trust_list.py","reason":"validity-only cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py","reason":"validity-only"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_verify_opcert.py","reason":"trust-list merge gate"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_verify_opcert_ac_coverage.py","reason":"trust-list merge gate"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py","reason":"signing not gated"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_binding_thread_propagation_ff4a.py","reason":"drop pin fixtures"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_rollback.py","reason":"drop pin fixtures"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py","reason":"drop pin references"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bugfix_size_gate_ad0d.py","reason":"validity-only trust"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_own_pub_resolution_d26a.py","reason":"own-key trust root removed"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_signature.py","reason":"vocabulary"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_own_principal_rotation_d909.py","reason":"deleted"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py","reason":"deleted"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90","parent_status_uuid":"359a167b-38f8-41aa-8cbf-f9c47ba8e303","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5220-052f-6d9c-4699","ticket_type":"story","title":"Op-cert verification is validity-only by default; no code path reads the repo-pinned trust file","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7abae9c2-c88c-410a-ad93-79cb355e868d","de1a0a66-f0e7-4caa-bb89-88b84be16b6f","c12407ec-f921-4d87-9791-9f7cb2119b51","6d801551-287f-49a8-a7b3-ae7e9bf2772c","637df7f9-85a8-444d-96a5-0374dd7d455d","359a167b-38f8-41aa-8cbf-f9c47ba8e303","2825ad26-8a86-44c1-9f9a-151ada70c6a5"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795118827110744991,"uuid":"a6aafe18-7c15-495c-a1e3-9dc377cbf967"}